{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 confirmed a parsimonious root cause. FastMCP builds the tool input model from each handwritten callable signature; because transition_ticket omits force/reason/caused_by/ref and claim_ticket omits force, undeclared payload keys are discarded before adapter execution. The adapter bodies independently forward only close_class or assignee, so a signature-only change would still fail. Runtime proof in an isolated tracker: live schemas omitted every field; real registered-tool capture received only current kwargs; an equivalent FastMCP tool with declared fields received exact sentinels; MCP ref selected HEAD instead of the requested older commit; and MCP caused_by closed without an edge while the library produced one. All four discriminating probes passed and temporary instrumentation was removed; the worktree is clean. The old negative force contract was deliberate in commit 95577d1960, but the signed 2026-08-18 operator ruling on restoring-shallow-blobfish explicitly rescinds it and establishes total lib/CLI/MCP parity with absent certification as the audit signal. This is therefore a defect/incomplete adapter wiring, not an unresolved design choice. Expected repair changes only the shared MCP adapter and its contracts; no caller depends on the stale omission because undeclared inputs are currently unreachable."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787085392492570001,"uuid":"85bec42d-930c-4e41-bf39-a47d41161108"}